WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.930
Picture a busy café.

2
00:00:01.930 --> 00:00:05.770
In one year it takes in 120,000.

3
00:00:05.770 --> 00:00:10.570
Food, staff, rent and energy cost 85,000.

4
00:00:10.570 --> 00:00:12.870
That leaves 35,000.

5
00:00:12.870 --> 00:00:15.330
The accounts call that a profit.

6
00:00:15.330 --> 00:00:18.390
Year after year, the café looks healthy.

7
00:00:18.390 --> 00:00:21.630
Yet an economist studies
the same café and says

8
00:00:21.630 --> 00:00:24.170
its real profit is zero.

9
00:00:24.170 --> 00:00:26.510
So why might a business
that brings in money

10
00:00:26.510 --> 00:00:30.130
every year still be making no real profit?

11
00:00:30.130 --> 00:00:33.980
In this mission, you'll work through
the café's year line by line,

12
00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:35.670
the way an economist would.

13
00:00:35.670 --> 00:00:38.510
Then you'll slide a
firm's price up and down

14
00:00:38.510 --> 00:00:40.620
and watch its profit rectangle grow,

15
00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:42.470
shrink and flip.

16
00:00:42.470 --> 00:00:47.230
Your mission: find out what an economist
counts that the accounts leave out.
